  "name": "api-gateway-troubleshooting",
  "description": "Diagnoses failing requests and deployment errors on Google Cloud API Gateway. Use when calls through a gateway return 4xx or 5xx errors, including 429 and other quota errors, time out, or fail a CORS preflight; when `api-configs create` fails with a service account, concurrency, or limit error, or `gateways create` or `gateways update` fails; when a custom domain, load balancer, or TLS finding involves a gateway; or when the user asks if Google is at fault. Don't use for Apigee, Cloud Endpoints, or GKE Gateway API. For OpenAPI errors from `api-configs create`, use api-gateway-openapi-spec-authoring; for setting up or changing API keys, JWTs, or quotas, use api-gateway-backend-security-and-rate-limiting; for MCP `/mcp` errors, use api-gateway-mcp-server.",
